  node [
    id 2752
    label "kbmg-0lpAOc"
    step 1
    date "2018-12-31T19:24:40Z"
    title "10-Minute Beginner Ab Workout for Women | Postpartum Ab Workout For Women"
    description "Follow along with this 10-MINUTE ABS workout video! I'll coach you through 9 core strengthening exercises perfect for beginners and postpartum moms looking to regain pelvic floor and lower abdominal strength.  &#10;&#10;This 10-Minute Beginner Ab Workout for Women is a great place to start because core strength is an essential foundation to all fitness levels. And great for injury prevention as well. A strong core is about so much more than aesthetics &#8212; it protects your other muscles {specifically your low back} as you move forward with higher-intensity workouts in the future.&#10;&#10;This workout was specifically designed as a beginner ab workout or postpartum ab workout for women, but these exercises are great for anyone looking to build a strong core foundation. Sometimes going back to the basics is the best thing you can do! &#10;&#10;&#128170; Looking for more Beginner Workouts at home? Download my FREE 30-Day Beginner Workout Plan Here: https://www.nourishmovelove.com/beginner-workout-plans/&#10;&#10;&#128073;Or find ALL of my Beginner Workouts in this YouTube playlist: &#10;https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLpa0d6IJAhbgwphHy5aYsls8E04t4o2lt&#10;&#10;&#128170; Looking for more Postpartum Workouts at home? Download my FREE 30-Day Postpartum Workout Plan Here: https://www.nourishmovelove.com/postpartum-workout-plans/&#10;&#10;&#128073;Or find ALL of my Postnatal + Postpartum Workouts in this YouTube playlist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLpa0d6IJAhbgM3v-uRntYjx7O00uMmGet&#10;&#10;&#10024; 10-Minute Beginner Ab Workout for Women &#10024; &#10;&#10;&#9654; EQUIPMENT: This 10 minute workout video uses a Pilates Sponge Ball, but you can also use a kids toy ball or throw pillow. The sponge ball helps to engage deep abdominal muscles (AKA the transverse abdominals) which can be overlooked in most ab workouts. &#10;&#10;&#9654; INSTRUCTIONS: Start wherever your fitness level allows, with the goal of working up to holding or performing each exercises for 45-60 seconds. Follow along with the video above, or use the exercise list below to move at your own pace. &#10;&#10;1. C-Shape Tucks into Ball&#10;2. Lying on Ball Toe Taps&#10;3. Lying on Ball Single/Double Leg Extensions&#10;4. Ball Between Knees Side to Side Drops&#10;5. Modified Side Plank Hip Lifts + Ball Squeeze&#10;6. Table Top Ball Between Knees 4 Squeezes + Mat Tap + Hold&#10;7. Table Top Roll Out&#10;8. Superman + Ball Press&#10;9. Glute Bridges + Ball Between Knees + Squeeze&#10;&#10;&#9654;FAQS&#10;&#10024; How many times a week should this be done?&#10;I suggest doing this 10-Minute Beginner Ab Workout for Women 2-3 times a week to tighten your belly after baby. &#10;&#10;&#10024;How soon after baby can I start these exercises?&#10;I always recommend chatting with your doctor or midwife before starting exercise postpartum. 6 weeks is a pretty common time frame, but every body is different. I personally started with these 7 Exercises for Postpartum Core Recovery + Diastasis Recti (https://www.nourishmovelove.com/postpartum-recovery-diastasis-recti-exercises/) about 12 weeks postpartum and progressed to the Beginner Abs exercises in this video a few weeks after that. &#10;&#10;&#10024; How do I know if I have Diastasis Recti?&#10;You can find out how to test yourself + some intro exercises to heal DR in this post: https://www.nourishmovelove.com/diastasis-recti-how-to-check-for-dr/&#10;_______________________________________________________________________________&#10;&#10;CONNECT WITH ME:&#10;Subscribe to Nourish Move Love and get my FREE Full Length Workout Video! &#10;https://www.nourishmovelove.com/subscribe&#10;&#10;Like us on Facebook!&#10;http://facebook.com/nourishmovelove&#10;&#10;Check us out on Instagram!&#10;https://www.instagram.com/nourishmovelove&#10;&#10;www.nourishmovelove.com"
