  node [
    id 2844
    label "2WxPfUBSpJo"
    step 1
    date "2020-10-27T08:33:44Z"
    title "5 Minute Standing Abs Workout Beginner for Women &#128073; NO JUMPING - AT HOME - NO EQUIPMENT &#128072;"
    description "5 Minute Standing Abs Workout Beginner for Women &#10;&#128073; NO JUMPING - AT HOME - NO EQUIPMENT &#128072;&#10;&#10;Today, we perform a beginner standing abs workout, with NO JUMPING, AT HOME, and NO EQUIPMENT required. This abs workout is part 3 of the 5 part fat blasting workout series from home.&#10;&#10;Standing ab exercises are suitable if you want to perform abdominal work and can't perform these exercises on the floor. Perhaps you have a back, neck, or knee issue preventing you from lying supine on the floor for ab workouts.&#10;&#10;Standing ab exercises are also low impact. Low impact workouts are suitable for many people. Low impact exercises protect your knees and your back. Also, jumping can be too aggressive, especially if you are just starting out as a beginner.&#10;&#10;If you are a beginner just starting out your workout regime, remember to take it slow and start with incremental progressions. If you want to get fit, you may like to join The 5 Minute Body. The program is designed to achieve your wellness goal with easy micro habits. The workouts coupled with simple nutrition advice are gentle and very easy to follow.&#10;&#10;Let's have a look at the exercises performed in this workout.&#10;&#10;Standing Oblique Crunch&#10;&#10;Stand with your knees slightly bent, your feet hip-width apart, and your hands behind your head. Shift your weight to the left leg, crunch to the right side, and bring your right knee up toward your elbow. Lower your right leg and return to the starting position. Switch legs and repeat until the set is complete.&#10;&#10;Standing Ab Crunch&#10;&#10;Stand with your feet slightly wider than shoulder-width apart. Engage your abs as you tilt your pelvis forward as if you're trying to bring your belly button to your spine and your hips up to your chest. Then, tilt your pelvis backward to stick out your butt as you bring your shoulders back and chest forward. Return to starting position to complete one rep.&#10;&#10;This workout is only 5 minutes, but if you have more time, you can repeat twice,&#10;There are 5 exercises performed back to back, with each ab exercise 60 seconds. If you need to rest between exercises, please press pause and resume when you feel ready.&#10;&#10;Timestamps of the exercises:&#10;00:00 Welcome&#10;00:48 Standing Oblique Crunch Right&#10;01:48 Standing Ab Crunch&#10;02:48 Standing Oblique Crunch Left&#10;03:48 Squat To Side Knee Lift&#10;04:48 Squat Side Bends&#10;05:50 Join The 5 Minute Body&#10;&#10;I hope you enjoyed this beginner standing abs workout. Please like the video and subscribe for more full body workouts to help you feel great!&#10;&#10;&#128315;  Ready to create the 5 Minute BODY? &#10;Subscribe: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCbGdNkuGB5e3cnf6xJWrluA?sub_confirmation=1&#10;&#10;&#128315;  Follow The 5 Minute BODY:&#10;&#10145;&#65039;  Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/the5minutebody/&#10;&#10145;&#65039;  TikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@the5minutebody?lang=en&#10;&#10145;&#65039;  Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/The5MinuteBODY/&#10;&#10145;&#65039;  Twitter: https://twitter.com/the5minute_BODY&#10;&#10;Helping to create your BEST self! Lots of love &#10084;&#65039;&#10;&#10;Disclaimer: Information provided in this video is of a general nature only and is for entertainment/educational purposes. We strongly recommend that you consult with your physician before beginning any exercise program. Performing any of these exercises is done so at your own risk.&#10;&#10;#absworkout #absworkoutforwomen #workout"
