  node [
    id 3097
    label "DDWg2XV22oc"
    step 1
    date "2022-05-10T15:00:40Z"
    title "4 Great Glute Exercises (read caption) #shorts"
    description "4 Exercises for Great Glutes&#10;&#10;SAVE THESE MOVES to try in your next workout &#128153; &#10;&#10;Good day fellow booty-building buddies! For this week&#8217;s workout Wednesday, I thought we could draw our attention to the derri&#232;re. &#10;&#10;The glutes are one of the biggest muscles in the body and are responsible for propulsion (i.e. sprinting, golf swing, kettlebell swing), for supporting strong posture by keeping us upright, supporting the low back and knees, and they are important for proper pelvic alignment.&#10;&#10;In addition to the aforementioned roles the glutes play, a well developed backside looks great on both men and women, right? &#9786;&#65039; So, if you want to build an impressive booty, I suggest you keep the following in mind:&#10;&#10;1. Training stimulus. It&#8217;s important, like most major muscle groups, to train the glutes in a variety of planes, with different tempos, and incorporating the principle of progressive overload.&#10;2. Outside of the gym. It would also behoove you to consider the other factors that contribute to muscle hypertrophy: quality of sleep, diet (are you eating to promote muscle growth- adequate protein consumption &#38; calories).&#10;3. Training frequency. If you are looking to build up a muscle group, it&#8217;s important that you train it often. I&#8217;d suggest you start anywhere from twice to five times a week. Mixing up the exercises as you like, but always making sure to thoroughly challenge yourself on each set. Mind muscle connection is key.&#10;4. Novelty. One of the best ways to break through plateaus is to incorporate novel movement patterns or exercises. Are you the kind of person who gravitates towards lighter-weight/ cardio-based classes? Try mixing some weight lifting routine into your routine and I&#8217;m sure you&#8217;ll be surprised at the results. The same goes for the avid gym-goer. Why not try some more functional moves to see how your body &#38; mindset shift.&#10;&#10;What are your thoughts on glute training? Do you currently have any of these moves in your rotation?&#10;&#10;Would you like to see these quick exercise videos turned into a series on here highlighting different muscle groups? Let me know down below!&#10;&#10;Xoxo,&#10;Ally&#10;&#10;&#10;MY WEBSITE: https://www.alexandratempletonfit.com/&#10;INSTAGRAM: https://www.instagram.com/allyt.fit/&#10;FACEBOOK: @alexandratempletonfit&#10;&#10;&#127916; POPULAR VIDEOS: https://www.youtube.com/user/AllyTCA/...&#10;&#10;&#128680;SUBSCRIBE to join the family! And if you enjoy these kinds of videos, it always means a lot when you like and share &#128591; &#10;&#10149; https://www.youtube.com/user/AllyTCA/...&#10;&#10;Music: Epidemic Sound &#10;&#10;Thank you for your support &#128515; It means so much and allows me to continue creating content on here for free."
    channel_title "Alexandra Templeton"
    channel_id "UCZu8wSlJpmQ22feBRKZozRA"
