    label "STIVazFs6Cg"
    step 1
    date "2022-03-25T07:05:27Z"
    title "7 MIN WORKOUT - Full Body HIIT to Burn Calories And Tone Up with No Equipment"
    description "Have you got 7 minutes of free time? Then come join me at this SUPER SWEATY full body intensive training! &#10;In fact, a HIIT cardio workout can burn a lot of calories in a short amount of time - and this session is your opportunity to check this yourself. During this training we are performing each exercise for 35 seconds with 7 seconds of active rest in between. For your convenience there is a sound at the end of each exercise that signals about ending. No equipment is needed, so it is a perfect variant for your at home training routine.&#10;&#10;IMPORTANT: Don't skip your WARM UP before the training (link is below). When you feel that it's getting too hard for you to continue this workout in fast rhythm - feel free to slow down and do all the exercises in your own tempo, but try not to stop unless you feel like you have to make a pause. It is a journey and you should always listen to your body and respect it's needs.&#10;&#10;&#128147; My Instagram: &#10;https://www.instagram.com/olyakrr/&#10;&#10;&#128147; If you want to help me and share this training with your friends (Much appreciated&#128522;) : &#10;https://youtu.be/STIVazFs6Cg&#10;&#10;&#128147; If you are just starting your training today - definitely start with a WARM UP. Warming up helps prepare your body for upcoming activity. A warmup gradually revs up your cardiovascular system by raising your body temperature and increasing blood flow to your muscles. &#10;https://youtu.be/uJy4Rnp36Bg&#10;&#10;&#128147; It is also very important to finish you training with a COOL DOWN - stretching is just perfect for that. In fact, stretching helps improve flexibility, increases range of motion and reduces the risk of injury caused by lesions of the connective tissue. By the way, it's a great for stress relief. &#10;https://youtu.be/-fnH0R_s0KE&#10;&#10;0:00 Start&#10;0:04 Burpees&#10;0:46 High Knees&#10;1:28 High Knee to Side Lunge&#10;2:10 Jump Squat to Twist&#10;2:53 4 Twist Jumps + 4 Plank Jacks&#10;3:34 Butt Kickers in Place&#10;4:16 Star Jacks to High Knee Jump&#10;4:58 Mountain Climbers&#10;5:40 Burpee to Star Jack&#10;6:23 Elbow Plank&#10;6:57 End&#10;&#10;#HIIT&#10;#WORKOUT&#10;#FULLBODY"
