  node [
    id 3541
    label "bh9qTlzFJgA"
    step 1
    date "2021-01-31T17:16:11Z"
    title "Beginner Ab Workout with Pilates Bar"
    description "Hello my CaliFitt Friends,&#10;&#10;     Today I have prepared an at home Pilates bar workout for you all to complete ! This exercise is designed to specifically target your abs ! You should work on your core muscles at least 2 to 3 times a week. Staying consistent with your ab workouts will help strengthen your core muscles, and in fact lead to them becoming stronger. Also, remember that all of our body shapes and structures are different, so there is not a set time frame in which we will all see results. It is just important to stay focused on your personal goals and growth throughout this process. Please, if you enjoy this video like, comment, share, and subscribe if you have not already done so ! Thank you all so very much for your love and support. We are on the road to 700 subscribers! This is so amazing ! Y&#8217;all keep up the good work and motivation ! #gymshark &#10;&#10;Workout clothes from @gymshark&#10;&#10;Below I have listed the music played within my workout video. I do not have or own any rights to the music within my video. Below is the requested and required information for both the artist and creators of the music.&#10;1. Good For You by THBD https://soundcloud.com/thbdsultan&#10;Creative Commons &#8212; Attribution 3.0 Unported&#8212; CC BY 3.0 &#10;Free Download / Stream: http://bit.ly/2PgU6Mu&#10;Music promoted by Audio Library https://youtu.be/-K_YSjqKgvQ&#10;2. Tonight by Rexlambo https://soundcloud.com/rexlambo&#10;Creative Commons &#8212; Attribution 3.0 Unported &#8212; CC BY 3.0&#10;Free Download / Stream: http://bit.ly/-tonight&#10;Music promoted by Audio Library https://youtu.be/Lct7aahfiMM&#10;&#10;Exercises that are performed within the workout video are listed below....&#10;1. Full body Squeeze &#10;2. Knee to Chest Ab roll&#10;3. (3) Leg drops to open V leg drop&#10;4.  (5) leg pulses into leg lift &#10;5. Slow leg drops to rise &#10;6. Knee to Chest Ab roll&#10;7. (2) leg drops to open V drop &#10;8. (5) leg pulses into leg lift &#10;9. Leg Drop (L) while (R) leg stays straight in the air ( do not bend either leg) &#10;10. Leg Drop (R) while (L) leg stays straight in the air (do not bend either leg) &#10;&#10;Stretching includes ...&#10;1. Forward stretch to knee position the come up (3x)&#10;2. Sumo Squat into Hamstring Leg Stretch (5x)&#10;3. Full body Pulse (5x)&#10;4. Full body stretch grab behind your knees&#10;5. Slowly Rise as you take a deep breath in &#38; breath out bringing your arms out beside shoulders (2x)&#10;6. Right leg Lunge ( perform to your comfort) &#10;7. Left leg lunge (perform to your comfort) &#10;8. Sumo Squat .. Stretching inner thighs (make sure to face palms of your hands outwardly &#10;9. Open legs wide / rotate feet to standing position &#38; go into a hamstring stretch &#10;10. Walk feet in &#38; complete a forward stretch &#10;11. Bow ! Great workout !"
    channel_title "CaliFitt"
    channel_id "UCfuMH8slSFz55YVaywY65Dw"
    fav_count -1
