    title "&#128293;Just Swing Arms to Flatten Stomach &#38; Lose Weight! Don't Underestimate This Sitting Exercise"
    description "Many people have experienced great results from my Shuai Shou exercise video. Shuai Shou exercise stimulates the muscles around your shoulder blades, and activates brown fat cells on your back. Today I am proud to present the great  Shuai Shou exercises sitting in a chair.&#10;&#10;This program is highly recommended not only for those who want to exercise comfortably, but also for those who really want to flatten your stomach.  The exercises in this video allow you to stimulate a variety of different muscles by changing the position of your hands. These exercises tighten your stomach more effectively by locking your lower body by sitting. Make sure to share it to your family and friends who have pain in their backs and lower backs  right away.&#10;&#10;*Please prepare a stable chair which does not move or rotate.&#10;&#10;03:50 Exercise starts.&#10;&#10;Practice Imi's Bigan yoga everyday with me and let everyone around you tell you &#34;you look brilliant and never get any older anymore! &#34;&#10;&#10; (Send me Before / After Pictures!)&#10;If you practice Imi's Bigan yoga, please take a picture as a record.&#12288;Please share your photos and videos with Imi by sending an email to this address. I will give you valuable personal advice to improve your practice to get even better results.&#10;bigan@herbyoga.jp&#10;&#10;If I would like to introduce what you share in my videos, I will ask for your consent in advance. Please understand that I am not able to answer all of your questions sent in emails.&#10;&#10;[Please click here for collaboration and work requests! ] &#10;info@herbyoga.jp&#10;&#10;[Disclaimer]&#10;This content is not intended to be a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Your viewing, commenting or subscribing to this YouTube channel does not create a counselor-client relationship. The statements made about specific products, exercise or massage are not to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent disease or symptoms. Imi's Bigan Yoga recommends that you consult your physician regarding the applicability of any recommendations and follow all safety instructions before beginning any exercise or massage program. When participating in any of this program, there is the possibility of physical injury. If you engage in this program, you agree that you do so at your own risk, are voluntarily participating in these activities, assume all risk of injury to yourself.&#10;&#10;[Image Source]&#10;By Anatomography - Anatomography 4.3, CC BY-SA 2.1 jp, https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=34066235&#10;CC 3.0, https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=238559&#10;&#10;By Anatomography - en:Anatomography (setting page of this image), CC BY-SA 2.1 jp, https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=22783765&#10;&#10;Anv&#228;ndare:Chrizz -CC 3.0, https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=239196&#10;https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=238610"
