  node [
    id 5193
    label "-bEy61DTGHQ"
    step 1
    date "2021-04-29T03:13:25Z"
    title "How Many Sets To Build Muscle AFTER 50?"
    description "How Many Sets To Build Muscle?...https://www.liveanabolic.com&#10;&#10;A good question I get asked a lot is, how many sets do I need to do to build muscle? There are quite a few different things I want you to think about when deciding how many sets you should be doing for the exercises in your workouts to build muscle. Let&#8217;s get started with those tips on how many sets to build muscle.&#10;&#10;Tip #1: WHAT IS YOUR FITNESS LEVEL. Are you a beginner, intermediate, or advanced? If you are a beginner, I typically recommend that you aim for 4-6 sets per muscle in your workouts. If you are intermediate, you should be doing 8-10 sets per muscle group. Finally, if you are advanced, you should be doing between 8 and 16 sets of each muscle group depending on the muscle group you are working.&#10;&#10;Tip #2: CIRCUIT TRAINING OR ANABOLIC TRAINING? When doing circuit-style training, there is typically no rest between exercises, and you are working multiple muscle groups. With this kind of training, you should be doing around 4 sets of each exercise depending on the number of exercises you are doing. This type of training is also great for losing weight and fat. Anabolic training is more for muscle growth and muscle building, instead of weight loss. You are going to do more sets with anabolic training because you rest after each set. I recommend you do 3-5 sets depending on your fitness level.&#10;&#10;Tip #3: HOW MANY REPS ARE YOU DOING IN EACH SET? WHAT TYPES OF SETS ARE YOU DOING? If you are doing a lot of reps, around 15 or 20, your muscles have more time under tension. This is going to really build up your lactic acid, which means you might not be able to do as many sets. If you are doing 8-12 reps, I would say to aim for 3-4 sets of each exercise.&#10;&#10;Tip #4: WHAT MUSCLE GROUPS ARE YOU WORKING? Big muscles require more sets to fatigue them. Leg workouts require more sets because they are big strong muscles. That is why people don&#8217;t like working legs because it takes more work to fatigue your muscles. Arms however, don&#8217;t need as much work to build the muscle.&#10;&#10;What is the secret answer? There is no simple answer, but that is what these tips are for. As you go to do your workouts, take into consideration all of these items. Adjust it to your fitness level and workout plan to get the best results and build muscle.&#10;&#10;Alright guys, that wraps up this video tutorial on how many sets to build muscle. Make sure to subscribe to our channel for more videos on how to build muscle and get back in shape at home.&#10;&#10;https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCvoih36zyNmXAbIQ_MaBsHw?view_as=subscriber&#10;&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-bEy61DTGHQ"
    channel_title "Live Anabolic"
    channel_id "UCvoih36zyNmXAbIQ_MaBsHw"
    fav_count -1
    view_count -1
    like_count -1
