  node [
    id 5211
    label "6WgkqwrZsEY"
    step 1
    date "2021-12-30T11:07:53Z"
    title "Did I Mention How Good Rebounding Is For Improving Bladder Control?"
    description "Firstly Can I ask a huge favour of you? Could you to like, comment and share my video. And if you like what you hear and see, would you mind subscribing to my Channel - this really helps me to grow and reach more and more people.&#10;&#10;Rebounding has so many health and wellness benefits. One benefit that was nearly overlooked is how your bladder control can improve over time, with gentle rebounding.&#10;&#10;While no one set out to help women with this weakness, many women have been sharing their delight at not having such a weak bladder since they have been rebounding.&#10;&#10;WARNING&#10;Now please be warned, this improvement doesn&#8217;t happen over night. It will come, slowly and surely over a prolonged time of gentle rebounding. Yes I said gentle rebounding, because with Rebounding you get excellent results with easy effort. &#10;&#10;Be gentle with yourself and allow yourself time. Rebounding is so effective that should you rebound too fast and too vigorously, you run the risk of causing strain to your very small and very deep muscles around your tummy, hips, upper legs and lower back. &#10;&#10;Remember that at all times you rebound at your own risk, and not everyone has the same results at the same time or in the same way. We are all individual and unique.&#10;&#10;Working Your Lymphatic System&#10;Rebounding Works your lymphatic system so well that you could also cause a massive clear out of toxins. While you think this is a good thing, when we over exert the lymphatic system too quickly, we can cause a massive reaction in our body and trust me, you don't want to have that experience either.&#10;&#10;Following Programmes Improves Success&#10;I set up EASY and Effective Rebound For Wellness Programmes  so that you have a programme to follow and you avoid any negative experiences when you rebound for your wellness. &#10;&#10;Research suggests that while you do need to exercise, you don't need to be killing yourself. Even gentle Rebounding works every cell and every muscles in your body and this is why rebounding can really benefit women who are going through the menopause or have gone through the menopause. &#10;&#10;Research also suggests that lack of incentive or motivation will cause you to fall away. That is why these programmes can be so helpful.&#10;&#10;To check out the Basic Rebound For Wellness Programme - click this link: https://retuningme.com/courses/rebound-for-wellness-basic-20-week-programme/&#10;&#10;Rebounding keeps your body toned with little work needed. It works those smaller muscles and all organs, including the bladder. &#10;&#10;Rebound For Wellness Programmes&#10;Most women who purchase the Rebound For Wellness Programmes tell me that they have the best results when they follow the programme - step by step as directed.&#10;&#10;You can begin to feel the benefits of this amazing system in a short time, and this could make you want to push on and do more than the programme suggests. Can I really encourage you to take your time, follow the programme and reap the best benefits.&#10;&#10;https://retuningme.com/courses/rebound-for-wellness-basic-20-week-programme/&#10;&#10;You don't need to be over exercising to get great results with Rebound For Wellness.&#10;&#10;Change Will Come&#10;The changes will come and I would be delighted to hear them.  You can read more about the benefits of rebounding for your wellness and my Rebound For Wellness Programmes over on my website - here&#8217;s the link:&#10;&#10;https://retuningme.com/rebound-for-wellness/&#10;&#10;Please Subscribe to my YouTube Channel and help me raise my profile and reach more women who suffer with leaky bladder and mild incontinence issues."
    channel_title "Nuala O'Connor @RetuningME"
    channel_id "UCp2Jpk00bkQ5U_WsFYeJHMA"
