  node [
    id 5232
    label "QbL1ksNO0Js"
    step 1
    date "2018-11-23T23:35:42Z"
    title "How to Do Oblique Crunches for Beginners - Get Well-Rounded Abs"
    description "Discover this great exercise &#38; these top fitness resources:&#10;Get our Fit Father 30-Day Fat Loss Program here &#8594; https://www.fitfatherproject.com/youtube-ff30x-program&#10;Get our Fit Father Old School Muscle Building Program here &#8594; https://www.fitfatherproject.com/youtube-osm-program&#10;&#10;Subscribe to our channel here &#8594; https://goo.gl/wxghQ5&#10;Our free resources:&#10;1-Day Weight Loss Meal Plan &#8594; https://www.fitfatherproject.com/youtube-1-dmp-optin&#10;24-Min Fat Burning Workout &#8594; https://www.fitfatherproject.com/youtube-24-min-optin&#10;5 Best Muscle Building Exercises &#8594; https://www.fitfatherproject.com/youtube-5-muscle-builder-optin&#10;&#10;One of the biggest mistakes a lot of people make when it comes to their core routine is neglecting the obliques. And it&#8217;s a big reason why people struggle to get those picture-perfect abs even after tons of effort. So to help you guys out, I created this quick guide on how to do oblique crunches for beginners so you can start rounding out your core routine in a much better way.&#10;&#10;Now, when it comes to properly training your obliques, the oblique crunches are really all you need. As you&#8217;ll discover in this video, simply adding a few sets of this exercise to your core routine will take care of the sides of your abs, and you&#8217;ll be on your way to having well-rounded abs.&#10;&#10;How to Do Oblique Crunches for Beginners&#10;&#10;When you look at the overall anatomy of the core, it&#8217;s really no surprise that our obliques don&#8217;t get worked in most common ab exercises. Since they&#8217;re on the sides of our lower torso, we need to modify the crunch to target each individually.&#10;&#10;The Setup (0:43)&#10;&#10;When it comes to doing oblique crunches properly, especially as a beginner, the correct setup is essential. Because as you&#8217;ll discover in this video and when you try them on your own, even the slightest change in your trunk or torso can shift the focus of the crunch away from your obliques.&#10;&#10;The Form Tutorial (1:26)&#10;&#10;As with most accessory exercises like the oblique crunch, the name of the game is staying slow and controlled. Because in addition to creating that constant tension throughout the motion, a slower pace makes it much easier to maintain the proper form.&#10;&#10;Sets, Reps &#38; Routine Recommendations (2:53)&#10;&#10;How to Build These Into Your Workout (3:22)&#10;&#10;If you feel your lifestyle could use an improvement, then check out our FF30X 30-Day Transformation Program at &#8594; https://www.fitfatherproject.com/youtube-ff30x-program&#10;If you want to start putting on muscle TODAY, check out our Fit Father Old School Muscle Building Program at &#8594; https://www.fitfatherproject.com/youtube-osm-program&#10;&#10;Your friends here at the FFP, &#10;&#10;-Dr. Balduzzi + The Men's Health Experts @ The Fit Father Project&#10;&#10;**Disclaimer: This information is for reference purposes ONLY and cannot replace personal information you can and should discuss with your Doctor. If you have any concerns about your health, you should see your Doctor immediately. Results vary by individual, so we do not guarantee you will get the same results as any shown here or on our website."
    channel_title "Fit Father Project - Fitness For Busy Fathers"
    channel_id "UCKvJ_vxZZoN5yeWBU2CVGcQ"
