    date "2022-06-23T11:44:46Z"
    title "TOTAL CORE/AB WORKOUT  ||  8 MIN  STANDING ABS || NO EQUIPMENT"
    description "Try this 8-minute standing AB workout. Engage your core and feel the tension within your abs.&#10;&#10;Exercises:&#10;&#128293;Alternating Standing Crunch&#10;Tip: Place your hands behind your head and perform a crunch, bringing your shoulder and head down toward the floor&#10;&#10;&#128293;Toe Touch&#10;Tip: Stand upright with your feet shoulder width apart, toes facing forward. Keep your legs straight whilst raising them up to meet with your hand.&#10;&#10;&#128293;Alternating Cross Body Crunch&#10;Tip: Engage your core muscles, open your elbows, keep your neck relaxed and your back straight&#10;&#10;&#128293;Arm Raise Crunch&#10;Tip: Starting with your arms raised, lower the arms and crunch into one leg.&#10;&#10;Subscribe to my channel: https://youtube.com/channel/UCspgttLbEbspsoNl5wFTn-A?sub_confirmation=1&#10;Instagram: instagram.com/trainsuz&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/groups/trainsuz&#10;TikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@trainsuz&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/trainsuz&#10;Contact (business inquiries):  hello@trainsuz.com&#10;&#10;&#10;Disclaimer&#10;&#10;If you are a complete beginner start with a pace you are comfortable with and then progress. Performing exercises out of your capability might strain your muscles and you may get injured.&#10;&#10;This channel offers health, fitness and nutritional information. You should not rely on this information as a substitute for, nor does it replace, professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. By performing any fitness exercises without supervision like with this video, you are performing them at your own risk. See a fitness professional to give you advice on your exercise form. TrainSuz will not be responsible or liable for any injury or harm you sustain as a result of this video.&#10;&#10;0:00 Introduction&#10;0:07 ALTERNATING STANDING CRUNCH&#10;1:06 TOE TOUCH LEFT LEG&#10;2:07 TOE TOUCH RIGHT LEG&#10;3:08 ALTERNATING CROSS BODY CRUNCH&#10;4:07 ARM RAISE CRUNCH RIGHT LEG&#10;5:08 ARM RAISE CRUNCH LEFT LEG&#10;6:08 CROSS BODY CRUNCH TO STANDARD CRUNCH RIGHT LEG&#10;7:08 CROSS BODY CRUNCH TO STANDARD CRUNCH LEFT LEG"
