  node [
    id 5391
    label "17zpuQqcmhc"
    step 1
    date "2022-07-04T13:21:38Z"
    title "FULL BODY BURN FAT WORKOUT|| 10 MINUTES ||  NO EQUIPMENT || APARTMENT FRIENDLY"
    description "Try this 10-minute FULL BODY workout. This workout requires no jumping so is apartment-friendly! :) &#10;&#10;45 Seconds on and 15 seconds rest.&#10;&#10;Exercises:&#10;&#128293;Squat Hold Punches&#10;Tip: Hold a squat position, ensuring legs are shoulder-width apart. Cross over and punch, making sure you are alternating each time.&#10;&#10;&#128293;Walk Outs&#10;Tip: Walk your hands forward while keeping your abs and back braced. Slowly walk your feet back to your hands.&#10;&#10;&#128293;Squat to reach&#10;Tip: As you reach the top of your stance, extend your arms directly overhead, ensuring your arms are close to your ears.&#10;&#10;&#128293;Squat into cross-crunch&#10;Tip: When coming back up from a squat position twist your body, and bring your left elbow down and across to your knee. Alternate each time.&#10;&#10;&#128293;High Plank&#10;Tip: Engage your abdominal muscles, drawing your navel toward your spine.&#10;&#10;&#128293;Toe Touches&#10;Tip: Crunch forwards, reaching up to your toes with your outstretched arms.&#10;&#10;&#128293;Single Leg drops&#10;Tip: Begin the exercise by lowering your right leg down slowly until it almost touches the ground, without changing the bend in your knee. Keep alternating legs.&#10;&#10;&#128293;Single Leg glute bridge&#10;Tip: While keeping your upper back in contact with the floor, lift your hips until your extended leg forms a straight line with your back.&#10;&#10;&#128293;Up and down fly&#10;Tip: Slowly exhale and lift your arms above your chest. Inhale and slowly lower your arms to your sides to the starting position.&#10;&#10;Subscribe to my channel: https://youtube.com/channel/UCspgttLbEbspsoNl5wFTn-A?sub_confirmation=1&#10;Instagram: instagram.com/trainsuz&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/groups/trainsuz&#10;TikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@trainsuz&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/trainsuz&#10;Contact (business inquiries):  hello@trainsuz.com&#10;&#10;&#10;Disclaimer&#10;&#10;If you are a complete beginner start with a pace you are comfortable with and then progress. Performing exercises out of your capability might strain your muscles and you may get injured.&#10;&#10;This channel offers health, fitness, and nutritional information. You should not rely on this information as a substitute for, nor does it replace professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. By performing any fitness exercises without supervision like with this video, you are performing them at your own risk. See a fitness professional to give you advice on your exercise form. TrainSuz will not be responsible or liable for any injury or harm you sustain as a result of this video."
