    step 1
    date "2022-04-19T13:14:11Z"
    title "Ep. 279: Kickboxing Combo Of The Day! &#128293; [Punch/Defense/Kick] #kickboxing #shorts #box45"
    description "LET'S CONNECT!&#10;Box45&#8482; Group &#128073; https://bit.ly/3jKGRSb&#10;Instagram &#128073; https://bit.ly/2FhltDr  &#10;Facebook &#128073; http://bit.ly/29in36f &#10;&#10;If you don&#8217;t have a punching bag you can still practice these combos by doing &#8220;shadow boxing&#8221;. Shadow boxing is a great cardiovascular training that can be done anywhere and anytime. No equipment is needed!&#10;&#10;KICKBOXING COMBO &#129354;&#10;&#128165; Cross - Hook - Cross &#10;&#128165; Lead Push Kick &#10;&#128165; Jump Back Kick&#10;&#10;===========================&#10;Box, Burn &#38; Tone At-Home! &#128293; Join our Facebook Group &#8220;At-Home Box45&#8482;&#8221; to claim your 1-WEEK FREE TRIAL! &#129354;  [The equipment is optional]&#10;===========================&#10;&#128680; BENEFITS OF KICKBOXING &#128680;&#10;&#10;1. Reduce Stress&#10;You can kick and punch your way to a stress-free zone within minutes of your high-energy kickboxing routine. The movements in kickboxing challenge several core muscle groups and will give you a total body workout, fast.&#10;&#10;2. Boost Confidence Levels&#10;According to studies, kickboxing helps you release endorphins which will give your mood a boost and help you feel more confident. Endorphins will also make you feel happier and more positive for several hours after the workout.&#10;&#10;3. Improved Coordination&#10;If you are suffering from posture problems and have poor coordination, you can strengthen your &#8216;core&#8217; and improve your reflexes and coordination skills. The speedy punches and kicks in the kickboxing routine will give you a chance to focus your energy to execute each movement successfully.&#10;&#10;4. Burn Mega Calories&#10;Some studies report that fitness kickboxing can burn up to 800 calories per hour, and you&#8217;ll be toning up your entire body as you rev up your metabolism. It&#8217;s a high-power cardio routine that is great for weight loss and getting you in shape, fast. &#10;&#10;5. Ideal Cross-Training Workout&#10;If you have been pounding on the treadmill for several weeks and need a break from your usual cardio routine, kickboxing is the perfect cross-training workout. You can add some weights by wearing wrist weights or ankle weights, or just putting on a pair of lightweight boxing gloves for extra resistance. Just one or two routines a week can help you break out of a fitness routine, fast.&#10;&#10;6. Energy Boost&#10;Kickboxing is a high-energy cardio routine that will give your body and mind a boost, and will increase your energy levels. You&#8217;ll be breathing hard and sweating out toxins; this process will give your energy levels a much-needed boost.&#10;&#10;Kickboxing workouts offer several benefits for your body and mind, and are a great choice for getting out of a fitness routine. Whether you are a fitness fanatic or just getting started with a workout routine, kickboxing can help you reach your fitness goals.&#10;&#10;====================&#10;&#127891; BIO: I am a certified Personal Trainer &#38; Nutrition Coach, Boxing and Kickboxing Trainer. I also have a background in Muay Thai Kickboxing and I hold a black belt in Taekwondo.&#10;&#10;#kickboxing #shorts #box45&#10;.&#10;.&#10;.&#10;.&#10;kickboxing, kickboxingtraining, muaythai, box45, boxing, boxingtraining, boxingworkout, martialarts, cardiokickboxing, tonemuscles, weightloss, weightlossjourney, fatloss, womenselfdefense,  selfdefensetraining, fitfam, grouptraining, teamtraining, virtualtraining, mma, thaiboxing, mixedmartialarts, selfdefense, knockout, kick, combatsports, trainer marcelo, kickboxing trainer, personal trainer, fitness trainer,"
    channel_title "Trainer Marcelo"
