    description "Box45&#8482; Group &#128073; https://bit.ly/3jKGRSb&#10;Instagram &#128073; https://bit.ly/2FhltDr  &#10;Facebook &#128073; http://bit.ly/29in36f &#10; &#10;Shadow boxing is a great cardiovascular training that can be done anywhere and anytime. No equipment is needed!&#10;&#10;SHADOW BOXING COMBO &#129354;&#10;&#128165; Jab - Cross - L. Hook [1-2-3] &#10;&#128165; Under - Under [U-U] &#10;&#128165; R. Hook - L. Uppercut [4-5]&#10;&#10;===========================&#10;Box, Burn &#38; Tone At-Home! &#128293; Join our Facebook Group &#8220;At-Home Box45&#8482;&#8221; https://bit.ly/3jKGRSb to claim your 1-WEEK FREE TRIAL! &#129354;  [The equipment is optional]&#10;===========================&#10;&#10;&#128680; BENEFITS OF BOXING &#128680;&#10;&#10;1. Reduce Stress&#10;You can punch your way to a stress-free zone within minutes of your high-energy boxing routine. The movements in boxing challenge several core muscle groups and will give you a total body workout, fast.&#10;&#10;2. Boost Confidence Levels&#10;According to studies, boxing helps you release endorphins which will give your mood a boost and help you feel more confident. Endorphins will also make you feel happier and more positive for several hours after the workout.&#10;&#10;3. Improved Coordination&#10;If you are suffering from posture problems and have poor coordination, you can strengthen your &#8216;core&#8217; and improve your reflexes and coordination skills. The speedy punches in the boxing routine will give you a chance to focus your energy to execute each movement successfully.&#10;&#10;4. Burn Mega Calories&#10;Some studies report that fitness boxing can burn up to 600 calories per hour, and you will be toning up your entire body as you rev up your metabolism. It&#8217;s a high-power cardio routine that is great for weight loss and getting you in shape, fast. &#10;&#10;5. Ideal Cross-Training Workout&#10;If you have been pounding on the treadmill for several weeks and need a break from your usual cardio routine, boxing is the perfect cross-training workout. You can add some weights by wearing wrist weights or hand weights, or just putting on a pair of lightweight boxing gloves for extra resistance. Just one or two routines a week can help you break out of a fitness routine, fast.&#10;&#10;6. Energy Boost&#10;Boxing is a high-energy cardio routine that will give your body and mind a boost, and will increase your energy levels. You&#8217;ll be breathing hard and sweating out toxins; this process will give your energy levels a much-needed boost.&#10;&#10;Boxing workouts offer several benefits for your body and mind, and are a great choice for getting out of a fitness routine. Whether you are a fitness fanatic or just getting started with a workout routine, boxing can help you reach your fitness goals.&#10;&#10;====================&#10;&#10;&#127891; BIO: I am a certified Personal Trainer &#38; Nutrition Coach, Boxing and Kickboxing Trainer. I also have a background in Muay Thai Kickboxing and I hold a black belt in Taekwondo.&#10;#boxingforbeginners #fitnessboxing #box45&#10;.&#10;.&#10;.&#10;.&#10;box, boxeo, boxing, boxing clinic, boxing class, boxing for beginners, boxing for fitness, fitness boxing, boxing training, boxing life, girls that punch, girls that box, youth boxing, boxing workout, boxing technique, trainer marcelo, box45, tone muscles, group training, team training, weight loss, weight loss journey, fat loss, weight loss motivation, in home session, online training, online coaching, home workout, virtual training, zoom training, in home training, personal training, small group training,"
