  node [
    id 5520
    label "Z4bCA4MRzZQ"
    step 1
    date "2022-01-13T15:19:48Z"
    title "This is a work of art..."
    description "&#9989; Subscribe to my main fitness channel: https://www.youtube.com/user/NalewanyjFitness&#10;&#10;Get Your FREE Workout &#38; Diet Plan:&#10;&#128221; https://www.SeanNal.com/freeplan&#10;&#10;Connect With Me:&#10;&#128073; https://www.instagram.com/Sean_Nalewanyj&#10;&#128073; https://www.tiktok.com/@sean_nalewanyj&#10;&#128073; https://www.facebook.com/SeanNalewanyjOfficial&#10;&#10;Premium Quality, Science-Based Supplements:&#10;&#128138; https://www.RealScienceAthletics.com/&#10;(Save 15% with coupon code YOUTUBE15)&#10;&#10;Thought this audio was funny and wanted to make a clip for it. Keep in mind though that the whole subject of &#34;good&#34; versus &#34;bad&#34; bodybuilding exercises can actually get very complex and involve a ton of nuance when you really break it down.&#8291; There are a wide variety of factors to consider, such as the muscle building goals of the individual, how a given muscle building exercise fits into an overall workout program as a whole, as well as what is precisely meant by the terms &#34;good&#34; or &#34;bad&#34;.&#8291;&#10;&#8291;&#10;But very quickly here's a brief summary...&#8291;&#10;&#8291;&#10;&#10145;&#65039; Dumbbell Press/Plate Press:&#10;&#10;Can't go wrong with a basic dumbbell press as a core chest building movement.&#10;&#10;Plate press is what I'd consider a legit &#34;bad&#34; hypertrophy exercise since it really doesn't load the pecs effectively and there are a million exponentially better options.&#8291;&#10;&#8291;&#10;&#10145;&#65039; Single Arm Pulldown/Behind The Neck Pulldown: &#10;&#10;This movement originates from @coach_kassem of @n1.education and is essentially the &#34;true&#34; version of a lat pulldown. What we traditionally call a &#34;lat pulldown&#34; (overhand with a straight bar) is more upper back focused.&#10;&#10;Behind the neck pulldown is its idiot brother and is not only worse from a hypertrophy standpoint but also increases injury risk. No good reason to do that, period.&#8291;&#10;&#8291;&#10;&#10145;&#65039; Incline DB Curl/Waiter Curl:&#10;&#10;Nothing magical about the incline dumbbell curl, but just wanted to show a solid, basic curling variation amongst the endless &#34;fancy&#34; curls we see all over IG nowadays.&#10;&#10;The waiter curl is not &#34;bad&#34; per se (it's a basic elbow flexion movement and so it'll still build biceps) but the alignment is not ideal and it's basically just a sub optimal way to train biceps.&#8291;&#10;&#8291;&#10;&#10145;&#65039; Dual Rope Pushdown/Reverse Grip:&#10;&#10;First saw this triceps exercise from Jon Meadows. Keep in mind that a single rope triceps pushdown is still effective, but dual gives you a bit more range and better arm path. Can also do it one arm at a time.&#10;&#10;Reverse pushdown is another one that isn't &#34;bad&#34; in the sense that it will still stimulate your triceps, but it's just a less effective version. No upside (triceps simply extend elbow in both cases), but has the downside of turning wrists into a potential limiting factor.&#10;&#10;#fitness #gym #workout #buildmuscle #bodybuilding"
    channel_title "Sean Nalewanyj Shorts"
    channel_id "UCtoCSRviHk6uFIb-zqeo4yQ"
    fav_count -1
    view_count -1
    like_count -1
