  node [
    id 5530
    label "frPfn46udHY"
    step 1
    date "2021-09-24T13:39:41Z"
    title "Athlean-X's Ridiculous Fat Loss Advice"
    description "Here's an example of why you probably shouldn't take fat loss advice from Athlean-X. Jeff Cavaliere ultimately promotes unrealistic body fat standards and in a recent post he has his &#34;Athlean range&#34; at 5-10% body fat. The vast majority of guys will NOT be able to maintain 6% body fat, 8% body fat or pretty much any body fat below 10% on a consistent basis. I don't care which Athlean-X workout or Athlean-X diet you follow, it's just not sustainable unless you're a genetic outlier or using PED's. You can definitely have a lean physique, but there's a big difference between a &#34;lean body&#34; and a &#34;shredded body&#34;. Try to take your body fat percentage too low and you'll be setting yourself up for a wide variety of physical and mental side effects.&#10;&#10;&#9989; Subscribe to my main fitness channel: https://www.youtube.com/user/NalewanyjFitness&#10;&#10;Get Your FREE Custom Workout &#38; Diet Plan:&#10;&#128221; https://www.SeanNal.com/freeplan&#10;&#10;Connect With Me:&#10;&#128073; https://www.instagram.com/Sean_Nalewanyj&#10;&#128073; https://www.tiktok.com/@sean_nalewanyj&#10;&#128073; https://www.facebook.com/SeanNalewanyjOfficial&#10;&#10;Premium Quality, Science-Based Supplements:&#10;&#128138; https://www.RealScienceAthletics.com/&#10;(Save 15% with coupon code YOUTUBE15)&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;#fitness #gym #workout #buildmuscle #bodybuilding #fatloss #burnfat #athleanx"
