    title "15 min ADVANCED Diastasis Recti Workout I Core Restore After Pregnancy I Abs After Baby I Liel Cheri"
    description "This ADVANCED Diastasis Recti workout is for mamas that have been already doing diastasis recti exercises and are feeling stronger to progress into more challenging exercises. &#10;Before practicing this video make sure you have done my level one + two and other diastasis recti workouts first.&#10;.&#10;Diastasis Recti Exercises save this AB Rehab / Diastasis Recti Exercises playlist:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLdCRrxKvCVCsvk8Mr7zjK9p0jBPInYwfO&#10;.&#10;I look forward to hearing from you in the comments how did you like these ADVANCED DIASTASIS RECTI workout to repair and strengthen your core after pregnancy. &#10;&#10;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#10;&#10;&#128293; &#128293; &#128293;&#128293;&#128293;&#10;8 Weeks Step by Step Program to Lose Baby Weight &#38; Recover Core and Pelvic Floor After Baby: &#10;Join the - CORE &#38; PELVEIC FLOOR RESTORE CLUB - &#10;https://lielcheridiastasisrecti.lpages.co/core-pelvic-floor-restore-club/&#10;.&#10;&#128293; 10 Exercises to AVOID with Diastasis Recti&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7KCY20kxL6g&#38;t=0s&#10;.&#10;&#128293; Grab a FREE copy of DIASTASIS RECTI eBook:&#10;https://lielcheridiastasisrecti.lpages.co/howtoflattenmommytummy/&#10;.&#10;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313;&#128313; &#10;Thank you for liking, subscribing and sharing! &#10;I love to get all of your lovely comments too! &#10;. &#10;Let`s connect: &#10;.&#10; www.lielcheri.com Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/thesassymommylifestyle&#10;Instagram: http://instagram.com/lielcheri&#8203;&#8203;&#8203; &#10;.&#10;.&#10;.&#10;Disclaimer: Consult with your physician before beginning any exercise program. You should be in good physical condition and be able to participate in the exercise. You should understand that when participating in any exercise, there is the possibility of physical injury. If you engage in this exercise, you agree that you do so at your own risk, are voluntarily participating in these activities, assume all risk of injury to yourself, and agree to release and discharge. &#10;.&#10;#diastasisrecti&#8203;&#8203; #diastasisrectiexercises&#8203;&#8203; #exercisesfordiastasisrecti&#8203;"
