  node [
    id 6606
    label "R6n7tHiSlzY"
    step 1
    date "2016-05-21T00:12:07Z"
    title "23 Isometric Core Exercises"
    description "23 Isometric Core Exercises&#10;&#10;Isometric Exercises are moves where you hold in a position under tension. And often when we think of &#8220;core&#8221; isometric moves, we think of Planks. And while Planks are great isometric core moves, they aren&#8217;t the only great Isometric Core Exercises.&#10;&#10;These 23 Isometric Core Exercises are a great way to build your core stability and strength so that your core works properly during heavy lifts. &#10;&#10;All of these moves also work your entire core &#8211; they work everything from your shoulders to your knees not just your abs.&#10;Because these moves improve your core stability, they can help you not only get a stronger, more toned middle, but they can also help you prevent and alleviate injury.&#10;&#10;Read more on the moves:&#10;&#10;http://redefiningstrength.com/10-isometric-core-exercises-to-improve-your-core-stability-and-strength/&#10;&#10;Check more of our core videos:&#10;&#10;Standing Ab and Core Exercises:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MWYM5u4DnV8&#10;&#10;Sit Up and Crunch Variations:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=804FkN60NsI&#10;&#10;Plank Variations:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bHOteDDCrLs&#10;&#10;Hanging Core Exercises:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5lE6I5R4pTk&#10;&#10;Advanced Core Exercises:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UxWkv1paQGc&#10;&#10;The 23 Isometric Core Exercises&#10;&#10;1. Banana (0:45)&#10;2. Boat (0:57)&#10;3. Dead Bug (1:10)&#10;4. Lower Ab Plank (1:22)&#10;5. Front Plank (1:34)&#10;6. Bull Dog (1:45)&#10;7. Superman (1:59)&#10;8. Posterior Plank (2:11)&#10;9. Push Up Holds Top (2:23)&#10;10. Push Up Holds Middle (2:28)&#10;11. Push Up Holds Bottom (2:36)&#10;12. Bird Dog Beginner (2:43)&#10;13. Bird Dog Advanced (2:55)&#10;14. Glute Bridge Hold (3:04)&#10;15. Bound Dog (3:15)&#10;16.Handstand Hold (3:27)&#10;17. Single Arm Handstand Hold (3:39)&#10;18. Wall Push (3:53)&#10;19. Dip Hold (4:08)&#10;20. Dip Hold L-Sit (4:21)&#10;21. Pull Up Hold Bottom (4:29)&#10;22. Pull Up Hold Middle (4:34)&#10;23. Pull Up Hold Top (4:44)"
    channel_title "Redefining Strength"
    channel_id "UCh2w-xqEwSz96sbn2afbOVQ"
