  node [
    id 6698
    label "ZOyAVh5Z_xc"
    step 1
    date "2015-10-14T21:03:30Z"
    title "3 Plank Exercises For Six Pack Abs"
    description "Learn the secrets to getting ripped abs from home:&#10;&#10;http://getrippedabsathome.com/absoluteworkout&#10;&#10;What's up my friends,&#10;&#10;Today I'm going to show you a bodyweight workout that you can use to get six pack abs. &#10;&#10;If you want to get a toned midsection without using fancy equipment, then look no further than planks. You can do planks at home, at the gym, or even during your lunch break at work. &#10;&#10;When performed correctly, planks will build sculpted definition in your abdominals by generating an isometric contraction. Whether you&#8217;re doing bodyweight or weighted workouts, there are three different muscle contractions that are associated with each movement.&#10;&#10;Concentric: whenever you lift a weight, you shorten the belly head of the targeted muscle. An example of a concentric contraction would be the curling movement for a biceps exercise. &#10;&#10;Eccentric: after the initial lift, you need to maintain control of the weight on the negative portion of each rep. This lengthens the belly of the muscle, which generates an eccentric contraction. An example would be descending your arms back down to a full extension when doing a biceps curl.&#10;&#10;Isometric: occurs when you stabilize a muscle group for an extended period of time. An example of an isometric contraction would be Plank or Wall Sits. &#10;&#10;You always want to integrate all three types of muscle contractions into your training regimen. This will force your body to adjust to new movements, which is key to building lean muscle mass. You never want to repeat the same workout over and over again. Your body will eventually acclimate to the workouts, which will cause your progress to become stagnant. &#10;&#10;In today&#8217;s workout, we&#8217;re going to do a plank variation for the upper abs, obliques, and lower abs. This will be a circuit workout, so you&#8217;ll be cycling through each exercise twice. &#10;&#10;If you want to build lean muscle from home, then grab a free copy of my &#34;Absolute Home Workout&#34; course:&#10;&#10;http://getrippedabsathome.com/absoluteworkout&#10;&#10;Although planks require minimal movement, they will produce maximum results. If you focus on executing proper form, I promise that you&#8217;ll feel the burn in your core. &#10;&#10;WORKOUT BREAKDOWN:&#10;&#10;Conventional Planks: targets the upper region of your abdominals. The key to this exercise is to keep your upper body completely straightened. This is a simple concept, but it&#8217;s not necessarily easy to do. When you reach the end of your set, you&#8217;ll be tempted to descend your hips to the ground. Don&#8217;t do it! This will only impede your results. Embrace the burn, and constantly try to push yourself past your current limitations.&#10;&#10;Side Planks: this is probably the best isometric exercise for your obliques. This exercise does require an element of balance, so make sure you focus on the form first. Make sure to keep your legs completely straightened, and place all your weight on your forearm and heels. If you do this correctly, you&#8217;ll also feel the tension in your front and middle deltoids. I like to put my opposite hand on my hip for stability purposes. When you&#8217;re done with the first set, immediately switch sides and repeat the same motion.&#10;&#10;Lower Ab Planks: most people completely neglect their lower abdominals. When you train them consistently, it will be the difference maker between six pack abs and eight pack abs. This exercise will build toned definition to your lower core. Place your hands underneath your tailbone and then fully extend both your legs. The key is to keep your heels roughly 2-3 inches off the ground at all times. This will place the maximum amount of tension on your lower abdominals, and you&#8217;ll love the results. &#10;&#10;In less than 5 minutes, we were able to generate an isometric contraction in all three regions of the abdominals. Start by doing 30 second intervals for each set, and then gradually increase your time as the weeks go by. Eventually, you&#8217;ll be able to do planks for minutes at a time. &#10;&#10;Always embrace the pain at the end of your sets, and constantly strive to break your current limitations. Leave a comment below if you want to see more workouts like this one.&#10;&#10;Train hard,&#10;Kiley&#10;&#10;For more free home ab workouts:&#10;&#10;http://getrippedabsathome.com/absoluteworkout"
    channel_title "Sculpted Muscle"
    channel_id "UCqmYK7nnLgHIC5qsZpzIXEQ"
    fav_count -1
    view_count -1
    like_count -1
    comment_count -1
    duration NAN
  ]
