  node [
    id 6807
    label "eZd0nvh7Uhs"
    step 1
    date "2019-06-23T23:38:22Z"
    title "Laying Windshield Wipers To Improve Your Core Strength - PearcePointers"
    description "Imagine having a 6-pack 30 days from today! Summer PowerAbs has 10 New Workouts...plus a new Level 3 which will give you a world-class challenge (trust me on this one!). F I'll show you how at https://www.pearcepointers.com/summerpowerabs-1a&#10;________________________________________________________________________________You may have noticed I am a big fan of core movements. Due to my gymnastics background, I have done a very large selection of different ab exercises. Because of my background, I believe your midline can never be too strong. Increasing your core strength will improve your gymnastics as well as weightlifting, along with giving you that 6-pack look everyone longs for.&#10;&#10;Today we are going over the Laying Windshield Wiper. This is one movement that my coach has me do every week. I like this one because it includes rotation so you may work your core in a way that you haven&#8217;t before if you've never done this movement. It'll work your abs and really fire your obliques. Along with that, you have to have good hamstring mobility to perform Windshield Wipers properly.&#10;&#10;The name is kind of funny, but you will notice if you do it right, you look like a set of Windshield Wipers!&#10;&#10;Here Are The 7 Steps You Need to Know For Laying Windshield Wipers&#10;&#10;1. Lay down flat on your back with your arms out to the side and legs extended. &#10;&#10;2. From here, lift your legs so that they are straight up in the air.&#10;&#10;3. While keeping your upper back flat on the ground and straight legs, lower both legs to the right.&#10;&#10;4. Keep your legs perpendicular to your body.&#10;&#10;5. Continue to lower your legs until they are six inches from the ground.&#10;&#10;6. Stop there and then bring your legs back up to the starting position and repeat on your left side.&#10;&#10;7. If you need to scale the movement, bend your knees or reduce the range of motion."
    channel_title "Kari Pearce"
    channel_id "UC6SkJ-l7I98tRMtwuSLStrQ"
    fav_count -1
    view_count -1
    like_count -1
    comment_count -1
    duration NAN
  ]
