  node [
    id 6904
    label "Uj4ffH5V1T8"
    step 1
    date "2021-07-08T12:41:09Z"
    title "30 Minute Testosterone Boosting Workout | No Repeat | Build Muscle"
    description "Funk and Angela take you through this 30-minute testosterone boosting workout using dumbbells and metabolic training.  This 30-minute testosterone workout is full body metabolic resistance workout designed to help burn fat, build muscle, boost growth hormone, and maximize testosterone levels, especially 30 minutes after the workout is complete&#10;&#10;FREE Protein Powder US ONLY &#8211; click the link below to get your FREE 7 Day Supply of LeanPro30 Grass Fed Whey Protein and 9 FREE BONUS programs today: https://funksupplementshop.com/leanpro30-free-7-day/&#10;&#10;My BEST Workout Programs&#10;&#61664; Best Program for Men Over 40: https://www.over40alpha.com&#10;&#61664; Best Program for Women: https://over40shred.com/WomenOfStrength&#10;&#61664; My Supplements: https://funksupplementshop.com/  (USE CODE: Funk10 FOR 10% OFF)&#10;&#61664; My Music: https://www.epidemicsound.com/&#10;&#10;My Social Channels&#10;&#61664; Subscribe to My YouTube Channel for FREE: https://www.youtube.com/funkroberts&#10;&#61664; Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/funkrobertsfitness/&#10;&#61664; Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/funkrobertsfitness&#10;&#10;Watch more of my videos! &#10;Subscribe and Click Notifications: http://www.youtube.com/subscription_center?add_user=Marcroops&#10;&#10;How to boost testosterone and growth hormone with this workout&#10;So, you want to cash in on that post-exercise testosterone spike? &#10;&#10;This workout is designed to help you increase your testosterone levels 30 minutes after the workout is done, while boosting your growth hormones both important aspects of building muscle and burning fat.&#10;&#10;Research finds that if you want to see increases in T levels, there are three key factors you need to consider:&#10;&#10;1. Train large muscle groups &#8594; Engaging multiple muscle groups at once means you&#8217;re recruiting more muscle mass; more muscle mass recruitment has been shown to be an important factor in testosterone release &#8211; 1, 3&#10;&#10;2. Lift heavy &#8594; The more muscle mass you have, the more testosterone your body releases. Low weight, high rep helps to tone muscle, but lifting heavy is the way to go if you want to add muscle - 1&#10;&#10;3. Shorten your rest periods &#8594; Rest period during resistance training is an important variable that can help increase anabolic hormone concentrations. Studies find that a shorter rest period (60 seconds) resulted in greater increases in GH concentrations, while a longer rest period (120 seconds) showed a greater testosterone response &#8211; 2&#10;&#10;4. 30 Minute Resistance Workouts &#8211; performing a 30 minute resistance training session increased testosterone for men by 21 percent and women 16 percent &#8211; 4 &#10;&#10;Basically, you want to maximize your work in the least amount of time, which means going heavy and going hard. The more damage you cause your muscles, the more opportunity they have to grow. There&#8217;s a time and place for light loads and low-intensity, but when you&#8217;re trying to jack up your testosterone levels it&#8217;s not the time for it. &#10;&#10;30 Minute Testosterone Boosting Workout Full Body NO REPEAT Workout&#10;Perform each exercise one after the other for 45 seconds of work followed 15 seconds rest for one round. 30 exercises with no repeat.&#10;&#10;1. Goblet Squat&#10;2. Reverse Lunge Right&#10;3. Reverse Lunge Left&#10;4. Stiff Legged Deadlifts&#10;5. Alternating Forward Lunge&#10;6. DB Push Ups&#10;7. Chest Press&#10;8. Floor Flyes&#10;9. Chest Press Rotations&#10;10. Alternating Neutral Grip Chest Press&#10;11. Single Arm Row Left&#10;12. Single Arm Row Right&#10;13. Pullovers&#10;14. Reverse Grip Rows&#10;15. Renegade Rows&#10;16. Arnold Dumbbell Shoulder Press&#10;17. Side Raise&#10;18. Standing Hammer Front Raise&#10;19. Bent Over Side Lateral Raise&#10;20. Single DB Shoulder Press&#10;21. Alternating Curls&#10;22. Drag Curls &#8211; Elbows back&#10;23. Hammer Curls&#10;24. Wide Curls&#10;25. Single Dumbbell Curls &#10;26. Crush Triceps Floor Press&#10;27. Skull Crushers&#10;28. Tate Press&#10;29. Triceps Floor Press&#10;30. Triceps Kickbacks&#10;&#10;WARNING: THE INFORMATION OFFERED IN THIS VIDEO IS OFFERED AS OPINION ONLY. ALWAYS CONSULT YOUR PHYSICIAN BEFORE TRYING ANY NEW DIET OR EXERCISE PROGRAM. THIS WORKOUT ROUTINE MAY NOT BE SUITABLE FOR YOU.  ALWAYS WARM UP PRIOR AND STRETCH AFTER YOUR WORKOUT SESSIONS&#10;&#10;References: &#10;1. Schroeder ET, Villanueva N, West DD, Phillips SM. Are acute post-resistance exercise increases in testosterone, growth hormone, and IGF-1 necessary to stimulate skeletal muscle anabolism and hypertrophy? Med Sci Sports Exerc. 2013, Nov;45(11):2044-2051.&#10;&#10;2. https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20555276/&#10;&#10;3. https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00423247&#10;&#10;4. https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00423247"
