    title "Best Fat Loss Bodyweight Workout (FULL WARM UP AND FOLLOW ALONG WORKOUT)"
    description "Funk and wife Angela take you through the best fat loss bodyweight workout for men and women. This is a metabolic body weight only workout which has a warmup and two 16 minute circuits.  Try this fat loss workout today.&#10;&#10;MEN - Alpha Workout and Nutrition Program - Start Your 30 Day Trial Workout Program for Men Over 40, 50 and 60 here: www.over40alpha.com &#10;&#10;WOMEN - Women Of Strength Program - Start Your FREE 30 Day Trial - https://over40shred.com/women-of-strength &#10;&#10;Watch more of my videos! &#10;Subscribe and Click Notifications: http://www.youtube.com/subscription_center?add_user=Marcroops&#10;&#10;Mega Shred Bodyweight  Workout&#10;&#10;Warm Up &#10;Perform each exercise for 30 seconds of work one after the other for 2 rounds&#10;1. Run and Gun Stationary Runs&#10;2. Twisters&#10;3. Hip Openers&#10;4. Lying Lumbar Twists&#10;5. Glute Hip Bridge&#10;&#10;Take a 30 Second Break and then go to circuit 1&#10;&#10;Shred 16 Circuit 1&#10;Perform each exercise for 40 seconds of work followed by 20 minutes one after the other for 4 straight rounds (no rest in between rounds) - Total Time = 16 minutes&#10;1.     Pulse Lunges (4 per side)&#10;2.     Push Up Jacks&#10;3.     Abs Crunch to Oblique Heel Touches (4 reps each)&#10;4.     Kicks Ups to Triceps Dips (4 reps each)&#10;&#10;Take a 60 second Rest and then move onto Circuit 2&#10; &#10;Shred-16 Circuit 2&#10;Perform each exercise for 40 seconds of work followed by 20 minutes one after the other for 4 straight rounds (no rest in between rounds) Total Time = 16 minutes&#10;1.     Wide-Reg-Close-Jump Squats&#10;2.     Abs Bicycles to Hip Raises (4 reps each)&#10;3.     3 Burpees to 10 High Knees&#10;4.     Jumping Jacks to Side Knees&#10;&#10;&#10;WARNING: THE INFORMATION OFFERED IN THIS VIDEO IS OFFERED AS OPINION ONLY. ALWAYS CONSULT YOUR PHYSICIAN BEFORE TRYING ANY NEW DIET OR EXERCISE PROGRAM. THIS WORKOUT ROUTINE MAY NOT BE SUITABLE FOR YOU.  ALWAYS WARM UP PRIOR AND STRETCH AFTER YOUR WORKOUT SESSIONS"
