  node [
    id 7557
    label "v1on079hNQg"
    step 1
    date "2014-11-21T18:33:25Z"
    title "Easy At-Home PLANK Workouts"
    description "&#34;YOU'RE ONLY ONE WORKOUT AWAY FROM A GOOD MOOD.&#34; &#10;&#10;-PLEASE READ* This video was based off of what I do with my own workout routine. The purpose of it is to simply help those of you out there who want to keep up with the many new wrinkles of health and fitness. Make sure you are able to perform these exercises before actually doing so to prevent any injury. If you have any history with back injuries, etc, make sure you ask your Doc first! You are responsible for your own health and knowing your own capabilities. Please train responsibly!&#10;&#10;*Forgive me for being a sloppy mess in this video. I must've done 100 of those jumping jacks before getting some good footage. rounds for filming purposes and was winded to say the least. Love this workout though because if you can consistently perform these movements in the shortest possible period of time you will get a KICK ASS workout! Enjoy guys! &#10;&#10;-Brett&#10;&#10;WORKOUT DETAILS:&#10;*You can do this on any soft surface&#10;*10-12 repetitions for each leg for all exercises&#10;*Make sure you are hydrated, and warmed-up before you start&#10;&#10;BEGINNERS: 3 ROUNDS&#10;ADVANCED: 5+ ROUNDS&#10;&#10;1. BLOOD-PUMPING JUMPING-JACK VARIATION (Full-Body)&#10;Start in a squat postion and explode thru your heels out in a jumping-jack motion, while coming back down into a squat position.&#10;2. GLUTE-BUSTING BRIDGE HOLDS (Glutes, Thighs, Core)&#10;Start on your back in a sit-up position, use your butt to bring your body up and hold for 2 seconds, back down.&#10;3. ONE-LEGGED BRIDGE HOLDS (Glutes, Thighs, Core)&#10;Same as the bridge holds but with only one leg.&#10;4. CORE-RIPPING PUSH-UP VARIATION (Full-body)&#10;Keeping your legs straight, walk on your hands into a push-up position, do a push-up and walk back into a stationary stance.&#10;5. AB-SHREDDING PLANK SHIFTS (Full-body) &#10;Get in a This will ignite a full-body burn great to end the workout with. &#10;&#10;**DON'T FORGET: if you really want to see gains in certain areas of your body, you need to first know your body, and then make sure you are getting the proper amount of food in your body based on your fitness routine! &#10;&#10;RECENT VIDEOS--&#10;Veggie-Stuffed Turkey Sliders&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uQEcJlyAVV0&#10;&#10;Protein-Trail Mix&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9rs1BYF3-CU&#10;&#10;Benefits of Lemon Water&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NepwQd778jk&#10;&#10;Exercise Ball Training&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t9Wpp8IEUVs&#10;&#10;At-Home Stairs Workout:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9rtOgzPWBag&#10;&#10;At-Home Lower-Back &#38; Core Workout:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fnmewstjYR8&#10;&#10;At-Home CrossFit Workout:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TxfRhsm559Q&#10;&#10;At-Home Jump Training Workout:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_nIa8nOBGgE&#10;&#10;MUSIC: Electric Bodega&#10;YOUTUBE&#10;https://www.youtube.com/user/Electricbodega&#10;FACEBOOK&#10;https://www.facebook.com/pages/Electricbodega&#10;SOUNDCLOUD&#10;https://soundcloud.com/electric-bodega"
