  node [
    id 8902
    label "wii-oa6DWYo"
    step 1
    date "2022-07-06T06:02:49Z"
    title "@A-Fit ISOMETRIC STRENGTH WORKOUT/FULL BODY STATIC TRAINING/Build MUSCLE STRENGTH/BURN CALORIES"
    description "Today is exactly the seventh day since I was tested positive with coronavirus.  I feel great, I feel that I have already recovered, but my body is still a little bit weak and I think that I will start returning to my workout  slowly so as not to hurt myself.&#10;That's why I decided to do this unusual workout today, which is suitable for people of all ages and any physiological condition.&#10;Our today's workout  will be a little bit unusual.  Our target today will not be any specific part of the body, but the whole body.  &#10;Today we will practice isometric (or static) exercises.&#10;If I could choose a few exercises from the abundance of Existing isometric  exercises, then I would choose these 12 as they cover almost every muscle group in your body.&#10;&#10;Isometric exercises (also known as static exercises) are performed by increasing tension in a muscle while keeping its length constant. Or in simple words , You  pick one position and hold it. For example, in a plank or wall sit, the muscles are working, but not actively changing lengths.&#10;If you want to burn calories without moving your muscles much, there is a way out &#8211; isometric exercises.&#10;&#10;In our today's program, I have selected 12 exercises that activate all the muscles in your body.  &#10; I hope that you will enjoy this workout and work with me till the end.&#10;&#10;&#10;To perform an isometric exercise, joint motion must be prevented. This can be achieved by pushing against an immovable object such as a wall or floor.&#10;Isometric exercises, also known as static strength training, are contractions of a particular muscle for an extended period of time. &#10;Every athlete wants to be able to generate a lot of explosive force. Isometric exercises, when added to a functional strength training program, have been shown to help athletes produce more speed and power. &#10;Studies have shown that that a 7 second muscle contraction increases your strength by about 5 percent.&#10;In addition, As you get older, you lose muscle tone, flexibility and the ability to digest essential amino acids, but regular isometric exercises can allow you to maintain your muscle strength. In fact, isometric exercises are a necessary kind of strength training for an older person who would like to stay healthy and mobile and for everyone else who would want to avoid muscular decline.&#10;Including isometric exercise in your training routine has the dual benefit of injury prevention and strength building.&#10;&#10; If you have or have had damaged muscles in your lifetime, this method can help you to rehabilitate your injury and reduce recovery time of your muscles. While it may seem like a good idea to just sit and rest, you may recover healing muscle more quickly by training. &#10;&#10;Isometrics are great at this because they don&#8217;t put too much strain on your muscles and joints.&#10;Isometric exercise activates or contracts the muscles without visible movement of the body. &#10;These exercises use self-resistance instead of weights/resistance bands to contract the muscle fibers.&#10;Isometric exercises are popularly practiced by physiotherapists for rehabilitation. They also reduce muscle fatigue, neck pain, and blood pressure and improve flexibility, core strength, and walking speed in elderly people &#10;&#10;Benefits Of Isometric Exercise&#10; &#8226; It helps strengthen the muscles.&#10; &#8226; It improves muscle tone.&#10; &#8226; Improves body posture and spine alignment.&#10; &#8226; It helps recover from injuries.&#10; &#8226; May help lower blood pressure.&#10; &#8226; It helps reduce arthritis pain.&#10; &#8226; May help improve heart function.&#10; &#8226; Increases resistance power.&#10; &#8226; It can be done anywhere and anytime.&#10; &#8226; It does not require any equipment. At most, a set of dumbbells is enough.&#10;Good for the elderly with limited movement.&#10;&#10;I really hope you will enjoy this unusual workout and don&#8217;t forget to Like and Subscribe at the end.&#10;Let&#8217;s Do this!&#10;&#10;#athomeworkout #strengthtraining #totalbodyworkout"
    channel_title "A-Fit"
    channel_id "UCfeqLZLfdbSu6d3cnGPqyaw"
    fav_count -1
    view_count -1
    like_count -1
    comment_count -1
    duration NAN
  ]
  node [
    id 8903
    label "kIbbkYKbYX8"
    step 1
    date "2022-07-06T20:42:30Z"
    title "10 MIN UPPER BODY AND CORE WORKOUT - At home - With weights"
    description "Wanted to make an upper body and core workout where you can work your arms as well as your abs! This workout is great for your upper body days and if you want to throw some abs in there as well! I am using 5 Ibs but you can use lighter or heavier. Which ever you prefer! I recommend starting lighter though if you are not used to weights. Throw in some water bottles! Those I feel are a great weight to start. If you prefer no weight at all, that is totally fine! Have fun! - AK &#10;&#10;Music from Epidemic Sound&#10;https://www.epidemicsound.com&#10;&#10;Top from CRZ Yoga on Amazon&#10;https://www.amazon.com/stores/CRZYOGA/page/F2232413-0F7D-4831-81A1-9FDFCFE5C54D?ref_=ast_bln&#38;store_ref=bl_ast_dp_brandLogo_sto&#10;&#10;Bottoms from Ododos from Amazon&#10;https://www.amazon.com/stores/ODODOS/page/4EE07D3A-483C-4E62-A43F-1E8D9A75F92A?ref_=ast_bln&#10;&#10;Follow me on Instagram&#10;https://www.instagram.com/abbykepfer/&#10;&#10;Disclaimer:&#10;Before proceeding in this workout, make sure to check your health before doing the exercises. If your at any risk with no supervision, this could lead to any injury or harm. I advise talking to your doctor or a fitness professional before continuing with this workout. Abby Kepfer will not be responsible or liable for any injury or harm you sustain from this video."
